rows.en:
And one after another, they all left the club room.
"Ah..."
A crushing despair seized {f:my|my} heart.{p}

...No, running now would be a bad idea{f:|}.
I'd {f:probably|surely} do better to watch a little longer and run once Kazama let his guard down.
That way my chances would be better, and it would be {f:safer|safer, surely}.{p}

...Maybe aliens really {f:do|do} exist after all.
Looking at Kazama, I somehow couldn't help starting to think so.
{f:Uh-oh.|Ugh, no...}
If I stayed with him too long, it felt like even {f:I|I}'d start going strange{f:|}.{p}

"Emergency transmission to the mothership! Emergency transmission to the mothership!
Request immediate response! Request immediate response!
☆★·☆··☆~☆"{p}

"...Oh, right. Ahahahaha..."
Our ride's coming?
Just what was supposed to be coming for us{f:|}?{p}

"{f:Gyah|Eek}★"
{f:I must have|I might have} jumped a good meter into the air{f:|}.
That's how startled I {f:was|was}.{p}

"Quit messing with me!"
{f:I|I} grabbed the ammonite {f:bastard|monster} in the doorway and yanked on its mask as hard as I could.
...But it wouldn't come off.{p}

...And then it lay there, not moving.
It isn't a mask?
If it isn't a mask... could it actually be real?{p}

{f:I|I} was desperate.
{f:I|I} must have been dozens of times more brilliant than any candidate's speech for student council president{f:.|.}
That's how well I think I pulled it off.{p}

...For now, I'll do my best to show proof that I'm a Sunbararian.
...But how?
That's it{f:!|!}{p}

"Kazama! Earlier, {f:I|I} showed you how to drop the ten-yen coin on the paper into the cup, didn't I?!
That's solid proof that {f:I'm|I'm} a Sunbararian, isn't it?!"
"...No good. Now that I think about it, even an Earthling might be able to do that."
...That's just too cruel.
It was Kazama who got it into his head that {f:I|I} was an alien in the first place{f:!|!}
He jumped to conclusions all on his own and brought this whole mess about{f:.|.}
Come to think of it, {f:I'm|I'm} the one being wronged here{f:!|!}{p}

"...Now. You peel yours off too."
With that, Kazama pointed at {f:me|me} and closed in.
The tentacles around his mouth wriggled and squirmed...
Even if {f:I|I} peeled off my face, there'd be nothing under it but muscle{f:!|!}
Are you kidding me{f:?!|?!}
What do I do?{p}What {f:the hell am I supposed to do|am I supposed to do}?!

"{f:Raaagh|Nooooo}!"
{f:I|I} slammed into Kazama with all my might.
Then I shut my eyes and flailed my arms around wildly.{p}

Suddenly Kazama let out a bizarre, incomprehensible shriek and toppled over with a thud.
Apparently {f:I'd|I'd} yanked on one of those tentacles.
So those weird tentacles sprouting from the mouth were the Sunbararians' weak spot{f:.|.}
...Even so, they're way too weak.
{f:These guys|These monsters} are this weak and {f:they|they} want to invade Earth? They must really look down on us Earthlings{f:.|.}{p}

{f:But|Still}, the danger has passed{f:.|.}
All I came here for was to hear scary stories from school, and before I knew it, {f:I'd|I'd} become a {f:hero|hero} who saved the Earth{f:.|.}
...But nobody will ever know.
{f:I|I} {f:am a lonely hero|am a lonely hero}.
{f:No|Yes}, in the end, that's all a {f:hero|hero} ever is{f:.|, isn't it?}{p}

Still, somehow I can't help feeling a little happy.
...Thinking back, the strange atmosphere hanging in the club room when I first walked in must have been coming from this Sunbararian{f:.|.}
I don't know if anyone will believe me, but I'll make this experience the seventh of the seven wonders.
Anyway, all's well that ends well.{p}

That's it!
{f:I'll make good use of|Let's make good use of} Kazama's corpse.
It's a little gross, but...{p}

Oh, to hell with it, whatever happens, happens!
{f:I|I} shoved my own head into that head.
There was a squelch, and its insides oozed out through the gaps.
...How utterly disgusting.
And that fishy stench.
But I can't afford to be picky{f:.|.}
My life is on the line{f:.|, after all.}
I can't see very well, but I can just make out what's going on through the gaps between the tentacles.
Oh, right{f:!|!} I'll take that patch-like thing Kazama had, too.{p}

A laser gun{f:!|...}
"I'm gonna die!"
This isn't some sci-fi movie, so why do {f:I|I} have to go through this{f:?!|?!}
Why are there Sunbararians in a place like this{f:?!|?!}
Those were my thoughts as {f:I|I} ran with all my might.{p}

Laser beam after laser beam shot past {f:me|me}.
If one hit, someone like {f:me|me} would be wiped out in an instant{f:.|.}
I have to get out of the school, no matter what!{p}

Once I was outside, the laser beams stopped chasing me.
But that didn't mean I could relax yet.
Because the schoolyard was crawling with Sunbararians too{f:.|...}
...Had the school been taken over by the Sunbararians{f:?|?}
{f:I|I} waved my hand and showed them the patch.
Then I walked slowly toward the school gate.{p}

First, I'll go to the police.
I'll go to the police and tell them about the Sunbararians{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} hurried to the nearby police box.{p}

"Eeeeeeeek!"
The street leading to the police box was crowded with people.
Sure enough, someone screamed.{p}

...Come to think of it, this is weird{f:.|.}
At first this head was fishy and creepy, but now it feels strangely natural.
As if it were {f:my|my} own head...
And when I really think about it, it's strange{f:.|.}
How {f:did|could} {f:my|my} head fit inside something only the size of Kazama's head?
It's the wrong size{f:!|!}{p}
